You can use the following function to convert a given binary string to a decimal number in Java:

```java
public static int binaryToDecimal(String binaryString) 
{ 
    double result = 0; 
    int lastIndex = binaryString.length() - 1; 

    // Iterating through the binary string 
    // from right to left 
    for (int i = 0; i <= lastIndex; i++)  
    { 
        int digit = binaryString.charAt(lastIndex - i) - '0'; 
        result += digit * Math.pow(2, i); 
    } 

    return (int)result; 
}
```

This function takes a binary string as input and converts it to a decimal number. It uses a for loop to iterate through the binary string from right to left. For each digit in the binary string, it converts the character to an integer by subtracting the ASCII value of '0'. Then, it multiplies the digit by 2 raised to the power of its position in the binary string (starting from 0) and adds it to the result. Finally, it returns the result as an integer.

